    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2 mt-2">Publishing</p>
      <h3 class="display text-2xl md:text-4xl mb-5 max-w-2xl">A deep Ghost ↔ Bonfire integration</h3>
      <p class="prose-body max-w-2xl"><span class="prose-body">Jacobin kept the Ghost workflow its editorial team already knew. We developed an open-source Bonfire extension around it, connecting publishing, membership, access and conversation without asking the team to maintain the same information twice.</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto mb-14">
    <div class="integration-points">
      <div class="integration-point">
        <h4 class="font-semibold">Articles stay in sync</h4>
        <p>Jacobin's archive can be imported in the background, while new articles and later edits arrive automatically. Titles, images, excerpts, dates and canonical links come across; unpublishing and republishing are reflected too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="integration-point">
        <h4 class="font-semibold">Membership becomes the sign-in</h4>
        <p>Readers use the email address they already have with Jacobin. Ghost confirms their membership and Bonfire sends a one-time sign-in link, so there is no second password or parallel member list to manage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="integration-point">
        <h4 class="font-semibold">Tiers carry their access with them</h4>
        <p>Ghost's public, member and paid visibility settings map to Bonfire boundaries. Membership tiers become circles that can unlock articles, discussions and private community spaces.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="integration-point">
        <h4 class="font-semibold">Every article opens into the community</h4>
        <p>Imported articles land in the group or topic Jacobin chooses. The embeddable comments widget connects the original Ghost page to that durable, federated discussion in Bonfire.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a href="/ghost/" class="btn-line mt-8 mb-8">Explore the full Ghost integration →</a>
  </div>

